    "recommendations": "Providing clearly visible address identification at the main entry point could improve responder navigation, particularly given the single access point and extended driveway length. Marking or confirming the driveway entrance to support apparatus turning and staging decisions may assist personnel arriving under emergency conditions. Keeping the driveway clear of obstructions along its full length would support unimpeded apparatus movement toward the main building. Given limited rear access and adjacent rocky terrain, identifying and communicating any available secondary approach or staging area to local emergency services in advance could facilitate more effective operational positioning during an incident."
